  "worked_solution": "First, from the diagram, notice that $∠CAB$ and $∠BAD$ are supplementary. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠CAB+m∠BAD & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠CAB+z & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠CAB & ={180}^{∘}-z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $△ABC$ is an isosceles triangle where $\\overset{―}{AB}≅\\overset{―}{BC}$, the base angles must be equal:\n\n$$\nm∠C=m∠CAB.\n$$\n\nFinally, since the interior angles of any triangle sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠CAB+m∠C+m∠B & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2m∠CAB+m∠B & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2({180}^{∘}-z)+{40}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {360}^{∘}-2z+{40}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2z & ={220}^{∘} \\\\ z & ={110}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
